<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady in thin business.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady in thin business.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in the markets of central India on Tuesday with demand matching arrivals and business slow.</p>
<p>Around 5.3 million hectares have been planted with soybean nationwide for the 1997/98 (November-October) season.</p>
<p>Soyoil solvent was up 100 rupees per tonne on limited supply at lower price level, while soyoil refined was steady. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in very thin trading. Soymeal yellow was $265-266 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for exports. Rapeseed extraction was $95-97 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 3,200-3,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
